      "item": "theoreticalsciences:unruh_accelerator",
      "title": "Unruh Accelerator",
      "text": "A storage ring whose electrons are accelerated so hard round their curve that, to them, the empty vacuum is warm.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the beam's Lorentz factor and the bending field. An electron of \u03b3 in a field B circles at r = \u03b3mc/eB with acceleration a = \u03b3\u00b2c\u00b2/r - and sees the vacuum at T = \u0127a/2\u03c0ck. The faster and tighter, the hotter; but synchrotron radiation drains the beam as \u03b3\u00b3B, and the cavities can only replace so much. Above 2 T the magnets saturate."
    },
